"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc=self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc||[]).push([[555],{6512(e,t,o){o.r(t),o.d(t,{_pageData:()=>a,default:()=>n});var r=o(641);const a=JSON.parse('{"path":"/woocommerce-pre-order/troubleshooting-faq.html","title":"Troubleshooting & FAQ","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"woocommerce-pre-order/troubleshooting-faq.md"}'),s={name:"troubleshooting-faq.md"},n=(0,o(6262).A)(s,[["render",function(e,t,o,a,s,n){return(0,r.uX)(),(0,r.CE)("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,r.Fv)('<h1 id="troubleshooting-faq" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#troubleshooting-faq"><span>Troubleshooting &amp; FAQ</span></a></h1><p>This section provides solutions to common issues encountered during configuration, integration, or store operations, along with answers to frequently asked questions.</p><hr><h2 id="_1-common-issues-resolutions" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-common-issues-resolutions"><span>1. Common Issues &amp; Resolutions</span></a></h2><h3 id="a-pre-order-button-not-appearing-on-product-page" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#a-pre-order-button-not-appearing-on-product-page"><span>A. Pre-Order Button Not Appearing on Product Page</span></a></h3><p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> The product displays a standard &quot;Add to Cart&quot; or &quot;Out of Stock&quot; button instead of &quot;Pre-Order Now.&quot;</p><ul><li><strong>Check Start Date:</strong> If you configured a <strong>Start Date</strong>, the pre-order buttons will only display <em>after</em> that timestamp. If the start date is in the future, the standard out-of-stock or add-to-cart layout is preserved.</li><li><strong>Check Status Toggle:</strong> Verify that the product-level <strong>Pre-Order Status</strong> toggle is set to <code>Enabled</code>.</li><li><strong>Stock Conflicts:</strong> If you checked <strong>Automatic Pre-Order (Auto-convert when out of stock)</strong>, the product must be set to <code>Out of Stock</code> in WooCommerce. If the product has physical stock (stock quantity &gt; 0), it will display standard purchase buttons.</li><li><strong>Theme Template Overrides:</strong> Custom product page templates may omit standard WooCommerce hooks (<code>woocommerce_before_add_to_cart_button</code>, <code>woocommerce_single_product_summary</code>). Revert to standard Storefront or Twenty Twenty-Four themes to isolate template conflicts.</li></ul><h3 id="b-stripe-automated-balance-charges-not-executing" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#b-stripe-automated-balance-charges-not-executing"><span>B. Stripe Automated Balance Charges Not Executing</span></a></h3><p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Pre-order products are restocked, but customer cards are not automatically billed for the remaining balance.</p><ul><li><strong>Stripe Webhook Connection:</strong> Automated payments require Stripe to communicate with your website. Check your Stripe Dashboard settings to verify that webhooks are active and successfully delivering events to your store.</li><li><strong>WordPress Task Backlog:</strong> The plugin queues automatic payments using standard background tasks. If payments are delayed, verify that your server&#39;s background task runner (cron) is working normally.</li><li><strong>Saved Payment Method:</strong> Auto-charging only functions if the customer&#39;s payment details were securely saved at the initial checkout. For guests or users who opted out of saving their card, they must pay the balance manually.</li></ul><h3 id="c-guest-users-cannot-access-their-pre-orders" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#c-guest-users-cannot-access-their-pre-orders"><span>C. Guest Users Cannot Access their Pre-Orders</span></a></h3><p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Guests see an error message or do not receive their email verification code.</p><ul><li><strong>Verify &quot;My Pre-Orders&quot; Page:</strong> Make sure the <strong>My Pre-Orders</strong> page exists in your WordPress admin panel under <strong>Pages</strong> &gt; <strong>All Pages</strong>. If it is missing, go to <strong>WooCommerce</strong> &gt; <strong>Pre-Order List</strong> &gt; <strong>Configuration</strong> &gt; <strong>Guest Settings</strong> and save the configuration to recreate it.</li><li><strong>Check Order Association:</strong> For security, the system only sends verification codes to emails that have active pre-orders. Double-check that a pre-order was placed with the exact email address the visitor is typing in.</li><li><strong>Host or Cookie Blocks:</strong> Some strict caching plugins or firewalls blocks custom cookie sessions. Verify that guest session tracking is excluded from your server&#39;s cache or optimization plugins.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="_2-frequently-asked-questions" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-frequently-asked-questions"><span>2. Frequently Asked Questions</span></a></h2><h3 id="can-i-set-different-pre-order-rules-for-individual-variations" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#can-i-set-different-pre-order-rules-for-individual-variations"><span>Can I set different pre-order rules for individual variations?</span></a></h3><p><strong>Yes.</strong> Under the <strong>Product Data</strong> box of a variable product, you can configure pre-orders on the parent level (which applies to all variations) or expand individual variations under the <strong>Variations</strong> tab to set separate availability dates, deposit structures, and prices per variation.</p><h3 id="how-are-taxes-and-shipping-calculated-on-partial-payments" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#how-are-taxes-and-shipping-calculated-on-partial-payments"><span>How are taxes and shipping calculated on partial payments?</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Taxes:</strong> Taxes are calculated during both stages of the transaction. The initial checkout calculates taxes on the partial deposit amount. The second checkout (balance payment order) taxes the remaining balance.</li><li><strong>Shipping:</strong> Shipping fees are charged during the initial pre-order checkout. The balance payment order does not charge shipping again, avoiding double charges.</li></ul><h3 id="what-happens-if-a-customer-misses-the-completion-window" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#what-happens-if-a-customer-misses-the-completion-window"><span>What happens if a customer misses the completion window?</span></a></h3><p>If <strong>Days to Complete</strong> is configured (e.g., 7 days) and a customer fails to pay their remaining balance before the deadline:</p><ul><li>The daily Action Scheduler sweep runs.</li><li>If <strong>Auto-Cancel Overdue Pre-Orders</strong> is enabled in the configuration, the pre-order status is changed to <code>Cancelled</code>, the inventory is returned to general stock, and a cancellation notice is sent.</li><li>If auto-cancel is disabled, the customer is marked as <code>Overdue</code>, but the order remains active for manual administrator resolution.</li></ul><h3 id="is-the-plugin-compatible-with-high-performance-order-storage-hpos" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#is-the-plugin-compatible-with-high-performance-order-storage-hpos"><span>Is the plugin compatible with High-Performance Order Storage (HPOS)?</span></a></h3><p><strong>Yes.</strong> The plugin is fully compatible with WooCommerce High-Performance Order Storage (HPOS), ensuring maximum order search speeds and stable database operations for modern storefronts.</p>',24)])])}]])}}]);